{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes"]]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This site uses the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-plugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". One command and it works,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because this is a Swift package with a single target."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In bigger projects the setup is not that simple. An Xcode project with many"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets, a framework whose docs live in a separate folder, a site that also"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carries onboarding pages. In those cases the plugin is not enough and you have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to run "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"docc"},{"type":"text","text":" yourself."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is how I do it. Every step is implemented in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"small package that only exists to be documented, so you can read the real"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"files instead of my snippets."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-two-halves","type":"heading","text":"The two halves"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DocC can render two kinds of content."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Generated API reference."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Types and functions with their doc comments. You"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never write these pages. The compiler describes your module in a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph"}]},{"type":"text","text":", one JSON file per module, and DocC turns it into pages."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Manual documentation."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Articles and guides you write as Markdown inside a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"documentation catalog"}]},{"type":"text","text":", a folder ending in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".docc"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Alone, neither is enough. The API reference says what a function returns, but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not why the feature exists. The guide explains the idea, but cannot link into"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the code. Putting them together is one flag. The rest is the work around it."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"1-Write-the-doc-comments","type":"heading","text":"1. Write the doc comments"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Generated pages are only as good as the comments in the code. A one line"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"summary, then details, then the parameters. Keep the summary to one sentence,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because DocC reuses it as the subtitle in every list."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"public"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"open"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols end up in the symbol graph, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never show up on the website."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"2-Add-a-catalog","type":"heading","text":"2. Add a catalog"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The catalog can live anywhere. It does not have to be inside a target, because"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you pass its path to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"docc"},{"type":"text","text":" directly:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["doc\/","└── GardenKit.docc\/","    ├── GardenKit.md      # landing page","    └── Guides\/"],"syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DocC flattens the catalog and finds pages by file name, so the folders are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only for your own order. Keep the file names unique."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One page becomes the front door. If you title a file with the module name in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"double backticks, DocC merges it into the generated module page:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"becomes the overview and your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Topics"},{"type":"text","text":" groups set the order of everything"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"below. That is what GardenKit and this site do."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"3-Get-the-symbol-graphs","type":"heading","text":"3. Get the symbol graphs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the generated half. Ask the compiler for symbol graphs while"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["xcodebuild build \\","    -scheme \"GardenKit\" \\","    -destination \"generic\/platform=iOS Simulator\" \\","    -derivedDataPath \"$build_dir\" \\","    -quiet \\","    OTHER_SWIFT_FLAGS=\"\\$(inherited) -emit-symbol-graph -emit-symbol-graph-dir $symbol_graphs_dir\""],"syntax":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three details matter here."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"generic\/platform=iOS Simulator"},{"type":"text","text":" builds for the simulator SDK without picking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a device, so codesigning never runs. A docs job has nothing to s"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\$(inherited)"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the flags the project already sets. If you drop it, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module compiles differently and you will not notice right away."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"build"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"docbuild"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"xcodebuild docbuild"},{"type":"text","text":" looks easier, but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"documentation for the whole dependency tree. If one of those dependencies has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Objective-C headers, DocC’s header pass can fail with duplicate symbol errors"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the build stops. A plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"build"},{"type":"text","text":" never runs that pass. It on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the Swift symbol graphs, which is all DocC needs. This took me a while to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"figure out."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"4-Keep-only-your-module","type":"heading","text":"4. Keep only your module"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The build writes a graph for every module it compiled, including"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dependencies. If you pass all of them to DocC, your dependencies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"your website:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["find \"$symbol_graphs_dir\" -type f -name '*.symbols.json' \\","    ! -name 'GardenKit.symbols.json' \\","    ! -name 'GardenKit@*.symbols.json' \\","    -delete"],"syntax":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both patterns are needed. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GardenKit.symbols.json"},{"type":"text","text":" has your own symbols."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GardenKit@Foundation.symbols.json"},{"type":"text","text":" is an extension graph, one per module you"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"extend. Delete those and every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"extension Date"},{"type":"text","text":" in your code qui"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disappears from the site."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"5-Put-them-together","type":"heading","text":"5. Put them together"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the command everything was preparing for:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["xcrun docc convert \"doc\/GardenKit.docc\" \\","    --additional-symbol-graph-dir \"$symbol_graphs_dir\" \\","    --fallback-display-name \"GardenKit\" \\","    --fallback-bundle-identifier \"com.example.gardenkit\" \\","    --output-dir \"$output_dir\" \\","    --transform-for-static-hosting \\","    --emit-digest"],"syntax":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--additional-symbol-graph-dir"},{"type":"text","text":" is the flag that merges the two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbol links in your articles resolve because of it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--fallback-*"},{"type":"text","text":" options give DocC the metadata Xcode would normally"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass for a target. A catalog you convert by hand has no target, so they are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"required. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--transform-for-static-hosting"},{"type":"text","text":" makes the output serv"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"file host, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--emit-digest"},{"type":"text","text":" writes the index the search needs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While writing, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preview"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"convert"},{"type":"text","text":". Same options,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localhost:8080"},{"type":"text","text":", and reloads when you save a Markdown file. It reads the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbol graphs from the folder you already created, so there is no rebuild."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"6-Serve-it","type":"heading","text":"6. Serve it"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the site is not at the root of the domain, pass the prefix or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"URL will be wrong:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["xcrun docc convert … --hosting-base-path \"docs\""],"syntax":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DocC does not write a root page either, so add a redirect:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["echo '<script>window.location.href += \"documentation\/gardenkit\"<\/script>' \\","    > \"$output_dir\/index.html\""],"syntax":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That is the whole pipeline. I keep it in a script with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-o"},{"type":"text","text":" fl"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the docs are previewed locally, with it they are converted for hosting. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full version is "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit\/blob\/main\/scripts\/generate_docs.sh","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". In CI the output is just a folder of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"static files, so publishing it is a copy."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Common-problems","type":"heading","text":"Common problems"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Topic reference 'Plant' couldn't be resolved."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The symbol graphs did"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not reach DocC. Check the path you passed, and that pruning did not delete"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"your own graph."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Extensions are missing."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Module@Other.symbols.json"},{"type":"text","text":" graphs were"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An internal type is missing."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Symbol graphs only contain public API."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Links","type":"heading","text":"Links"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit","isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GardenKit"}],"overridingTitle":"GardenKit"},{"type":"text","text":", the example, with the full script"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/formattinnt","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-symbolkit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", the symbol graph format"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/releasenotes\/doccpipeline"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/DoccPipeline"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Building one documentation site from two sources: the API reference the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compiler generates, and the articles I write by hand."}],"sampleCodeDownload":{"action":{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit","overridingTitle":"View GardenKit on GitHub","type":"reference","isActive":true},"kind":"sampleDownload"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/AsyncSequenceOperator","doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/DoccPersonalSite"],"anchor":"Patch-Notes","title":"Patch Notes","generated":true}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","images":[{"type":"card","identifier":"card-docc.svg"}],"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Haydar Karkin"}],"title":"Combining Generated and Manual Docs"},"references":{"https://github.com/haydarKarkin/GardenKit/blob/main/scripts/generate_docs.sh":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit\/blob\/main\/scripts\/generate_docs.sh","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit\/blob\/main\/scripts\/generate_docs.sh","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"in GardenKit"}],"title":"in GardenKit","type":"link"},"https://github.com/haydarKarkin/GardenKit":{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit","checksum":null,"type":"download"},"https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-docc-plugin":{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-plugin","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-plugin","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"swift-docc-plugin","type":"text"}],"type":"link","title":"swift-docc-plugin"},"https://www.swift.org/documentation/docc/formattinnt":{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/formattinnt","url":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/formattinnt","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Formatting your documentation content","type":"text"}],"type":"link","title":"Formatting your documentation content"},"doc://ReleaseNotes/documentation/ReleaseNotes/DoccPersonalSite":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/releasenotes\/doccpersonalsite","identifier":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/DoccPersonalSite","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a personal site actually needs, and how far DocC gets you with each of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"those things."}],"title":"Turning DocC into a Personal Site","images":[{"identifier":"card-site.svg","type":"card"}],"role":"article"},"doc://ReleaseNotes/documentation/ReleaseNotes":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/releasenotes","identifier":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Senior iOS Developer. I build iOS apps that keep working as they grow."}],"title":"Haydar Karkin","role":"collection"},"https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-docc-symbolkit":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-symbolkit","title":"SymbolKit","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-symbolkit","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SymbolKit"}]},"card-site.svg":{"identifier":"card-site.svg","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/ReleaseNotes\/card-site.svg","svgID":"bg","traits":["1x","light"]},{"url":"\/images\/ReleaseNotes\/card-site~dark.svg","svgID":"bg","traits":["1x","dark"]}],"alt":"A browser window with a header bar and two cards","type":"image"},"card-docc.svg":{"identifier":"card-docc.svg","variants":[{"svgID":"bg","traits":["1x","light"],"url":"\/images\/ReleaseNotes\/card-docc.svg"},{"svgID":"bg","traits":["1x","dark"],"url":"\/images\/ReleaseNotes\/card-docc~dark.svg"}],"alt":null,"type":"image"},"card-async.svg":{"identifier":"card-async.svg","variants":[{"svgID":"bg","traits":["1x","light"],"url":"\/images\/ReleaseNotes\/card-async.svg"},{"svgID":"bg","traits":["1x","dark"],"url":"\/images\/ReleaseNotes\/card-async~dark.svg"}],"alt":"An input timeline throttled to one element per window","type":"image"},"doc://ReleaseNotes/documentation/ReleaseNotes/AsyncSequenceOperator":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/AsyncSequenceOperator","type":"topic","title":"Writing Your Own AsyncSequence Operator","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/releasenotes\/asyncsequenceoperator","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What it takes to add an operator like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"throttleFirst"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"how to test it without waiting for real time to pass."}],"kind":"article","images":[{"identifier":"card-async.svg","type":"card"}]},"https://www.swift.org/documentation/docc/":{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DocC documentation"}],"type":"link","title":"DocC documentation","url":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/"}}}